  "id": "031",
  "title": "Quartet",
  "subtitle": "\"They needed a fifth musician for a twelve-city tour. By week three I had four men in my bed and a rock album to finish.\"",
  "penName": "Juniper Cash",
  "genre": "reverseHarem",
  "hook": "Midsummer Descent lost their touring violinist to a motorcycle accident three weeks before their North American tour. I was Juniper Cash, a twenty-eight-year-old session violinist in Nashville with two hundred and eleven session credits and exactly nine thousand dollars in savings. The band's manager offered me the tour. Twelve cities. Forty-two days on a bus with four men. The singer was Gideon. The guitarist was Rook. The bassist was Colm. The drummer was Vesper. By week two I was too tired to pretend. By week three the Moon Goddess of rock music had chosen me four times.",
